{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1522215-changeling-reproduction-new-fae-souls-or-reincarnation","id":1522215,"title":"Changeling reproduction: new fae souls or reincarnation?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-07T06:26:34-07:00","id":1522215,"title":"Changeling reproduction: new fae souls or reincarnation?","content":"I've been doing some research and couldn't find an answer. If two changelings have a child, that child will not always be a changeling, right? But in the case that they are, is the kid a new fae soul, or just another reincarnation of a changeling?<br /> <br /> I think it gets even more complicated when talking about the Sidhe. If two arcadian Sidhe have a child (like I saw that king David wants to), and that child IS a changeling, will they be a newly formed Sidhe soul? Will they be the possible reincarnation of another arcadian Sidhe? Could they still be considered an ARCADIAN Sidhe? Or would they be autumn Sidhe? Or even a new, third kind of Sidhe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26311-ulbrecht","name":"Ulbrecht","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26311_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-07T08:06:29-07:00","id":1522220,"title":"","content":"Look, their faerie half might have been another changeling's, now another changeling's relative is called a kitain, I think, and doesn't necessarily become a changeling, as he has to have a certain way of thinking and believing in the supernatural. About the Sidhe, I think that a new type wouldn't born from the crossing of two different Sidhe, I believe that the difference between the two is in the way each one faces the world, which makes autumnals more resistant to banality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-07T19:21:12-07:00","id":1522251,"title":"","content":"I'm not talking about the Kitain, but of the ones that have become a changeling. <br /> <br /> About the Sidhe, I'm not thinking of a crossing between different Sidhe, but of the child of two arcadian Sidhe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26311-ulbrecht","name":"Ulbrecht","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26311_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-07T20:14:07-07:00","id":1522252,"title":"","content":"I do not think there is a canonical answer. So whatever answer you pick is one that fits your ideas about the setting, fairy lore, and the needs of your game.<br /> <br /> As for me, I default heavily into as much actual fairy lore as much as I can in my interpretation of the setting. Most players, in my experience, have a setting that often does not match well to actual fairy lore. That's OK. You pay your money, so you decide in your chronicle. One of the things fairy lore tells us is that fairies seem to have a hard time reproducing on their own. That's why they often kidnap human children and midwives. So while I do not believe there should never be any new fairy births, they should be extremely rare.<br /> <br /> I also believe that humans/changelings give birth humans. Any fae part of a new changeling is not the result of biology in the Autumn World. The changeling part must come elsewhere and then merge with the human. So that implies it is almost always an existing fae spirit that is looking for a home. <br /> <br /> If there is such a thing as a &quot;new fae soul&quot;, it has to come outside human biology. It has to have its origins in the Dreaming. And if that is true, how does it get birthed because it isn't by any mating by humans/kithains/changeling? That doesn't mean it's impossible. But I would place any brand new fae spirits to have to be born solely by chimerical beings in the Dreaming. Perhaps only in Arcadia itself in the modern day.<br /> <br /> So my answer to this question is that it's only existing fae spirits that are being reincarnated. If you want an actual new fae spirit to be generated and arrive, that should be its own special plot that has impact in the setting. It doesn't need to be a special thing related to the coming of Endless Winter or other prophecies, or be a unique event. But it should be an exceedingly rare event that has a major impact when it does happen. Perhaps it is a mystery even to the changelings when it does happen.<br /> <br /> I have no doubt that there will be many posters subsequent to me that disagree. They have different ideas on what the merger between the human self and fae being means, how much actual fairy lore is relevant to the game and setting, and what they think would be cool. And that's OK.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-07T20:52:43-07:00","id":1522254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1522215-changeling-reproduction-new-fae-souls-or-reincarnation?p=1522252#post1522252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not think there is a canonical answer. So whatever answer you pick is one that fits your ideas about the setting, fairy lore, and the needs of your game.<br /> <br /> As for me, I default heavily into as much actual fairy lore as much as I can in my interpretation of the setting. Most players, in my experience, have a setting that often does not match well to actual fairy lore. That's OK. You pay your money, so you decide in your chronicle. One of the things fairy lore tells us is that fairies seem to have a hard time reproducing on their own. That's why they often kidnap human children and midwives. So while I do not believe there should never be any new fairy births, they should be extremely rare.<br /> <br /> I also believe that humans/changelings give birth humans. Any fae part of a new changeling is not the result of biology in the Autumn World. The changeling part must come elsewhere and then merge with the human. So that implies it is almost always an existing fae spirit that is looking for a home.<br /> <br /> If there is such a thing as a &quot;new fae soul&quot;, it has to come outside human biology. It has to have its origins in the Dreaming. And if that is true, how does it get birthed because it isn't by any mating by humans/kithains/changeling? That doesn't mean it's impossible. But I would place any brand new fae spirits to have to be born solely by chimerical beings in the Dreaming. Perhaps only in Arcadia itself in the modern day.<br /> <br /> So my answer to this question is that it's only existing fae spirits that are being reincarnated. If you want an actual new fae spirit to be generated and arrive, that should be its own special plot that has impact in the setting. It doesn't need to be a special thing related to the coming of Endless Winter or other prophecies, or be a unique event. But it should be an exceedingly rare event that has a major impact when it does happen. Perhaps it is a mystery even to the changelings when it does happen.<br /> <br /> I have no doubt that there will be many posters subsequent to me that disagree. They have different ideas on what the merger between the human self and fae being means, how much actual fairy lore is relevant to the game and setting, and what they think would be cool. And that's OK.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, following this line of thought, how would the &quot;next generation&quot; o Sidhe be - assuming the Endless Winter haven't arrived? Will the arcadian ones cease to be? Will they be forced to accept the changeling way, and so there will be only autumn Sidhe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26311-ulbrecht","name":"Ulbrecht","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26311_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-07T23:46:32-07:00","id":1522256,"title":"","content":"Does anything actually stop an Arcadian Sidhe from coming back the same way they did the first time? The dreaming isn't sealed any more, it seems like they'd just have to put a lot of effort into it because it's not as easy without the changeling way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-08T12:54:26-07:00","id":1522280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daniel Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1522215-changeling-reproduction-new-fae-souls-or-reincarnation?p=1522256#post1522256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anything actually stop an Arcadian Sidhe from coming back the same way they did the first time? The dreaming isn't sealed any more, it seems like they'd just have to put a lot of effort into it because it's not as easy without the changeling way.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I understand, no arcadian Sidhe has reincarnated yet after the Ressurgence, so the whole idea that they don't know what happens after their deaths. They don't even know if they go or not to the Dreaming after they die.<br /> <br /> If I'm not mistaken, King David wanted to have an heir. How would that happen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26311-ulbrecht","name":"Ulbrecht","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26311_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-08T16:30:46-07:00","id":1522281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulbrecht</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1522215-changeling-reproduction-new-fae-souls-or-reincarnation?p=1522254#post1522254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, following this line of thought, how would the &quot;next generation&quot; o Sidhe be - assuming the Endless Winter haven't arrived? Will the arcadian ones cease to be? Will they be forced to accept the changeling way, and so there will be only autumn Sidhe?</div> </div> </div> </div>I never personally liked the idea that the Sidhe had disappeared in the Late Middle Ages and only came back after the Apollo Moon Landing. This is very strange lore to me because actual fairy lore has nothing like that. I don't mind the idea that the Fae are dwindling and there are less of them every year because magic is dying. That was the theme of the Time-Life series of Enchanted World books that I read as a kid, and it makes sense to me. But there continued to be reports of fairies, including beings like the Sidhe, even up to today. If it were up to me, the Sidhe would have been like every other Kith. I think its a mistake of the setting that they weren't.<br /> <br /> But there's no way to answer your question by the setting because we have no idea of the population of Sidhe that were expelled versus how many have already incarnated. And we never will (and the rules shouldn't ever tell us IMO). While in theory at some point Arcadian Sidhe should run out, we don't know if that will be in one day, one year, one century, one millennia, or whatever. Nor can we say that the &quot;distribution&quot; of Arcadian Sidhe has to proceed on a linear basis or logorithmic or random or any other trend. It can be anything. So the real answer is what do you want it to be?<br /> <br /> If it was my chronicle, my personal preference would likely be that Arcadian Sidhe decline over time, getting rarer and rarer, but never quite ending until the arrival of Endless Winter. If I want to run a chronicle where Endless Winter happens, I might explain that no one has seen a new Arcadian Sidhe come out of Chrysalis in several years. If I want to hint that Endless Winter is near but won't happen in the course of my chronicle, I would just have it be very rare, only heard of as rumors from distant Freeholds. If I don't care about the proximity of Endless Winter, I'd still have Arcadian Sidhe be fairly common, but probably in decline relative to Autumn Sidhe.<br /> <br /> Ask yourself what are your chronicle needs, and you should be able to determine the answer for your own games. That's my advice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}